The National Party is expected to win the sixth seat in Queensland, thus giving the Coalition 39 seats and outright control of the Senate. Labor won the final seats in New South Wales and South Australia, giving it 28 seats. The Greens have only one definite new seat, in Western Australia. The last seat in Tasmania is a close contest between the Greens and Family First, with the Greens' [[Christine Milne]] expected to win.

